  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{5}{4})(y-0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=-3$ and $k=0.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(-3,0).$",
